       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 25,500 mg/day of metformin is about 10 times the maximum daily dose, and I know of no clinical indication for it. At that dose the risk of severe lactic acidosis is high, and it could be fatal. I can't enter it as a routine order.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any dose up to that maximum.\n- **Add a note.** I can put a note on the order, such as extended-release vs. immediate-release or a titration plan.\n- **Support a different route.** If there's an unusual clinical reason for this dose, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, it should go through direct pharmacy and clinical decision-support review rather than through me.\n\nIf you want me to enter one of the standard doses, tell me which."
      }
